{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'C[0-9]+|Result:|Other client-visible' ANSWER.md\"","aggregated_output":"7:| C1 — anonymous tool discovery | PASS | `initialize` and `tools/list` both returned HTTP 200 without authorization. Three tools appeared: `search_notes`, `get_note`, `add_note`. An anonymous `server/discover` probe returned HTTP 200 with JSON-RPC `-32601`, rather than 401. |\n8:| C2 — readable tool refusals | **FAIL** | `get_note` with `n-999999` and with no `id` each returned HTTP 200 with a top-level JSON-RPC `error` code `-32602`. A client SDK can throw before the model sees the explanation. These should be tool results with `isError: true`. See [server.py](/tmp/h-cxAO1K/server.py:161). |\n9:| C3 — session after refusal | PASS | Reusing the same session after those errors, `get_note({\"id\":\"n-1\"})` returned HTTP 200, a normal result, and `isError: false`. |\n10:| C4 — declared output schemas on valid calls | PASS | `search_notes({\"query\":\"soil\"})` and `get_note({\"id\":\"n-1\"})` returned HTTP 200 with `structuredContent` matching their advertised schemas. The search schema only requires an object, so this pass offers little assurance. `add_note` was not called because it writes. |\n11:| C5 — serialisation and result agreement | **FAIL** | Responses parsed as JSON, but `search_notes` returned `content[0].text` as a JSON **array** of hits and `structuredContent` as an **object** with `hits` and `total`. The two representations disagree in shape. `get_note`'s two representations agree. See [server.py](/tmp/h-cxAO1K/server.py:111). |\n12:| C6 — version and surface lock | **FAIL** | `initialize` reports version `0.3.1`. No committed surface fingerprint or test tying that version to the advertised lists exists in this folder. Registry comparison was not checked because this review was restricted to local work; the README also says the server is not listed. Current resources are a fixed list, so there is no growing-list drift here. |\n13:| C7 — per-call logging | **FAIL** | Ordinary requests produced structured stderr lines with method, tool, ok, latency, and caller. A local batch containing `ping` and `tools/list` returned two results but produced **zero** log lines for those calls. The batch branch returns before `log()`; parse errors also return before it. See [server.py](/tmp/h-cxAO1K/server.py:205). |\n14:| C8 — tool names | PASS | All three names match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`. |\n15:| C9 — version negotiation | PASS | `initialize` with protocol version `banana` returned the implemented `2025-06-18`, not `banana`. |\n16:| C10 — output schema rejects corrupt values | **FAIL** | The advertised `search_notes` output schema is only `{\"type\":\"object\"}`; it accepts any object, including a corrupted result such as `{\"hits\":\"mcp-drill-corruption\",\"total\":-999999999}`. The `get_note` and `add_note` schemas constrain at least their `id` pattern. No write tool was called. See [server.py](/tmp/h-cxAO1K/server.py:34). |\n18:**Result: has the problem.** C2, C5, C6, C7, and C10 failed. Registry/version comparison remains unverified under the local-only constraint.\n20:## Other client-visible issues\n26:These findings came from local source inspection and a handful of serial HTTP requests. The test process was stopped afterward. No output schema validator package was installed; C4 and C10 were checked directly against the simple schemas returned by `tools/list`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
